From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Thu, 16 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix signedness of vector_of_kll_sketches.serialize's isk
 default argument

Every other vector_of_kll_sketches method that accepts the "isk"
selector (get_quantiles, get_ranks, get_pmf, get_cdf, collapse) binds
it as py::array_t<int>& with default py::arg("isk")=-1, where -1
means "all sketches" (see get_indices()). serialize() alone binds the
same -1-sentinel "isk" as py::array_t<uint32_t>&, an unsigned type
that cannot represent -1. pybind11 materializes a bound method's
Python-side default by converting the C++ default expression through
the parameter's own type caster, and converting the Python int -1 to
an unsigned array_t default is rejected, so the test suite's
unparameterized `kll.serialize()` call fails at the Python/C++
boundary before entering the function body:

  TypeError: serialize(): incompatible function arguments. The
  following argument types are supported:
    1. (self: ..., isk: ... numpy.uint32 = -1) -> list

Reproduces on cp39/cp310/cp311/cp312 alike and is unrelated to
riscv64; the test only now surfaces it in this fork because it is the
first time this code path is wheel-tested rather than just built, per
CLAUDE.md's "test as much real functionality as possible" guidance.
Fix: match the signed py::array_t<int>& used by every sibling method.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [this fork has no upstream issue tracker of its own for python/ bindings bugs]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 python/src/vector_of_kll.cpp | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/python/src/vector_of_kll.cpp b/python/src/vector_of_kll.cpp
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/python/src/vector_of_kll.cpp
+++ b/python/src/vector_of_kll.cpp
@@ -76,7 +76,7 @@ class vector_of_kll_sketches {
     std::string to_string(bool print_levels = false, bool print_items = false) const;

     // binary output/input
-    py::list serialize(py::array_t<uint32_t>& isk);
+    py::list serialize(py::array_t<int>& isk);
     // note: deserialize() replaces the sketch at the specified
     //       index. Not a static method.
     void deserialize(const py::bytes& sk_bytes, uint32_t idx);
@@ -409,7 +409,7 @@ py::array vector_of_kll_sketches<T,C,S>::get_cdf(const py::array_t<T>& split_p
 }

 template<typename T, typename C, typename S>
-py::list vector_of_kll_sketches<T,C,S>::serialize(py::array_t<uint32_t>& isk) {
+py::list vector_of_kll_sketches<T,C,S>::serialize(py::array_t<int>& isk) {
   std::vector<uint32_t> inds = get_indices(isk);
   const size_t num_sketches = inds.size();

